  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (HVAC fan and pump)",
  "applies_to": "LS Electric LSLV-H100+ HVAC fan and pump inverters using the integrated RS-485 port with COM-02 set to BACnet.",
  "summary": "The H100+ has BACnet MS/TP on its integrated RS-485 port (COM-02 Int485 Proto = 4 BACnet). The fixed object list has writable AVs for frequency reference, ramps, PID reference/feedback, command timeout and three analog outputs, BVs for run/stop, reset and relay outputs, AIs for drive monitors and trip/warning words, and BIs for drive state and terminal I/O. Several objects (AV 9, AI 28, BI 31-35) belong to the extension I/O.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 237000,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "From the LSLV-H100+ User Manual (2nd edition, July 2026), section 7.4.5 Object Map (PDF pp359-363). Only the BACnet objects are listed; the Metasys N2 map that follows is left out.",
    "AV 8 and AV 9 are both printed with the object name CommAo2; AV 9 is the analog output 3 (extension I/O) setting.",
    "AV 2, AV 3 and AV 4 can be written in AUTO mode only. AV 4 cannot exceed DRV-20 Max Freq and is used when DRV-07 Freq Ref Src = Int 485.",
    "To drive the analog outputs from AV 7-9, set OUT-01 AO1 Mode, OUT-07 AO2 Mode and APO-30 AO3 Mode to 16-18 (Comm Output 1-3).",
    "To drive relays from BV 6-11, set the relay function (OUT-31 to OUT-39) to 0 (None).",
    "AI 24 RunTimeMin is printed with units Day; the doc's description says run time by minute. The printed MSI is listed as MI; MSV as MV."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "LSLV-H100+ Series User Manual, 7.4 BACnet Communication",
    "doc_number": "H100+ Programming Manual v8 (2nd edition)",
    "revision_date": "2026-07",
    "url": "https://www.lselectricamerica.com/api/v1/fo/ctpApi/fileDownUrl?filePath=CTP%2FManual%2F1684678068%2FH100%2B%20Programming%20Manual_v8_260730.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set COM-02 Int485 Proto = 4 (BACnet), the MAC address in COM-01, baud in COM-03 and the device instance in COM-84/COM-85. Set DRV-06 Cmd Source = Int 485 and DRV-07 Freq Ref Src = Int 485, then write BV 2 to run, BV 1 to stop and AV 4 for speed. Read BI 2, AI 5, AI 4 and BI 4.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 2",
        "name": "RunForwardCmd",
        "why": "Run forward command (True = run)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "StopCmd",
        "why": "Stop command (True = stop)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 4",
        "name": "CommandFreqSet",
        "why": "Frequency reference, Hz"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 4",
        "name": "ResetFaultCmd",
        "why": "Reset a tripped drive"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 2",
        "name": "RunningForward",
        "why": "Running forward status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 5",
        "name": "OutputFreq",
        "why": "Output frequency, Hz"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "OutputCurrent",
        "why": "Motor amps"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 8",
        "name": "OutputPower",
        "why": "Output power, kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 4",
        "name": "Tripped",
        "why": "Any active trip"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 30",
        "name": "Warning",
        "why": "Any active warning"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "DRV-06 Cmd Source must be 3 (Int 485) for the run/stop BVs and DRV-07 Freq Ref Src 6 (Int 485) for AV 4. The drive has Hand-Off-Auto keys; AV 2-4 can be written in AUTO mode only.",
    "heartbeat": "AV 1 CommTimeoutSet (0.1-120 s) and MV 1 LostCommand (0 None, 1 Coast Stop, 2 Decel Stop, 3 Hold Input, 4 Hold Output, 5 Lost Preset) set the lost-command time and action. The manual's speed-command-loss parameters (Lost Cmd Mode / Lost Cmd Time in the PRT group, default 1.0 s) also apply to integrated RS-485.",
    "remote_sensors": "AV 6 PIDFeedbackSet lets the BMS write the PID feedback and AV 5 PIDReferenceSet the PID setpoint.",
    "setup": [
      "COM-02 Int485 Proto = 4 (BACnet). COM-01 Int485 St ID is the MAC address, 0-127.",
      "COM-03 baud: 9600 (default), 19200, 38400 or 76800 bps for BACnet. COM-04 sets parity (D8/PN/S1 default, even or odd).",
      "COM-83 BAC Max Master, 1-127, default 127.",
      "Device instance = COM-84 x 1000 + COM-85 (defaults 237 and 0, so 237000).",
      "COM-86 BAC PassWord (default 0 = ignored) protects ReinitializeDevice warm/cold start.",
      "With COM-96 PowerOn Resume = Yes, written AV values survive a power cycle."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "BV 1 StopCmd, BV 2 RunForwardCmd and BV 3 RunReverseCmd are separate commands; write the stop BV to stop.",
      "ReadPropertyMultiple is not in the listed services; poll with ReadProperty."
    ]
  },
